export anchor ZenMailStyle:
    number: 402
    screen: EmailClient
    name: Zen mail
    idea: One message at a time on sumi black, set in a large quiet serif with ink brush strokes and an enso, a short numbered queue to the side, and a single vermilion seal for the one action that matters.
    base: dark
    palette:
        sumi: #121110, the page
        stone: #1a1917, the style sheet
        wash: #2c2a26, dividers and the enso stroke
        paper: #ece4d4, text and the brush stroke
        grey: #a9a193, meta and queue subjects
        mist: #6c665c, underlines only and never text
        seal: #e5664f, the Reply seal, new marks, the current item bar and the focus ring
        onSeal: #1a0703, text on the seal
        moss: #a7c08f, the starred mark
    type:
        A mincho serif stack, Hiragino Mincho ProN, Yu Mincho, Songti SC,
        Noto Serif, Georgia, at a 16px base with 1.8 leading. The subject is
        56px at 400, the letter 24px with 2.0 leading, queue senders 16px
        and bold when unread, small section words 14px with very wide
        tracking. A sans stack, Hiragino Sans, Yu Gothic, Noto Sans,
        system-ui, sets meta and the small marks at 12 to 14px.
    layout:
        Three bands across the width. A 72px band holds Brightwork Mail
        written vertically top to bottom with a small vermilion square
        stamp under it. A 300px queue column, ruled off by one thin line,
        reads Inbox, twelve, then an underlined field reading seek, then a
        numbered list 01 to 06 with the sender, the subject and time on one
        line and a small mark below. The current item has a short
        vermilion brush bar to its left and a vermilion number. The folders
        and labels sit at the very bottom as small plain links. The stage
        fills the rest with wide margins. A large faint enso circle sits
        behind the top right. It reads one of six in spaced letters, then
        the subject very large, From and To with the time in small sans, a
        tapered brush stroke, the letter in large serif and a dash before
        Clients. Actions are a square vermilion seal for Reply, then Reply
        all, Forward, Snooze and Archive as underlined words, and a quiet
        line naming the next message. On a phone the brand runs across the
        top, the queue comes first, then the message.
    spacing: An 8px unit used generously. 96px above the message, 40px around the brush stroke, 64px before actions.
    density: Very sparse. One message fills the stage and the queue is six quiet lines.
    corners: None on panels. The seal has slightly uneven corners from 3 to 7px, and swatches are pebble shaped.
    borders: One 1px wash line between queue and stage. Secondary actions are words with a thin underline.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        No icon set. The brush stroke and enso are decoration. Marks are a
        glyph plus a word, a dot plus new, a six point star plus starred,
        a hollow diamond plus enclosed.
    focus: A 1px paper outline offset 6px with a vermilion ring outside it. Fields turn their underline vermilion.
    tone: Unhurried and lowercase, such as one of six, seek, and Next, when you are ready.
